=== layout: two-panels

# Umbilical Blood Sampling (PUBS)

@left

- *Percutaneous umbilical blood sampling*: fetal blood from the umbilical cord
- Cells can be used for chromosome testing
- Used later in pregnancy for selected indications
- CVS/amniocentesis usually preferred for chromosome diagnosis

@right

![Lecture diagram](assets/lect10d-chromo_aneuploid/image_021.png)

@citation

https://publications.smfm.org/publications/589-society-for-maternal-fetal-medicine-clinical-guideline-6/

=== layout: two-panels

# Newborn Screening

@left

- Tests after birth can identify conditions that benefit from early treatment
- *PKU*: phenylketonuria
- A recessive disorder of phenylalanine metabolism
- Blood is collected after birth
- An abnormal screen needs follow-up testing

@right

![Lecture diagram](assets/lect10d-chromo_aneuploid/image_022.png)

=== layout: reference

# For Reference: Newborn Screening

@body

{table-style=comparison column-widths="1,4"}
| Group | Examples |
| --- | --- |
| [*Metabolism*]{color=#24578F} | PKU, methylmalonic acidemia, MSUD, tyrosinemia, citrullinemia, MCAD deficiency |
| [*Hemoglobin*]{color=#24578F} | Sickle cell disease, hemoglobin SC disease, beta thalassemia |
| [*Hormones*]{color=#24578F} | Congenital hypothyroidism, congenital adrenal hyperplasia |
| [*Other*]{color=#24578F} | Galactosemia, biotinidase deficiency, cystic fibrosis, SCID, Pompe disease, MPS I, X-linked adrenoleukodystrophy, spinal muscular atrophy |

Panels vary by screening program.

