=== layout: two-panels

# You Can Shop for Eye Color

@left

- *The Fertility Institutes* and *Simple Fertility* advertise eye-color selection
- IVF produces embryos; genetic testing helps choose which to transfer
- Embryo selection, not gene editing
- Predicted eye color; no guarantee

https://www.simplefertility.com/eye-color-selection

@right

*If eye color, what else?*

- Other diseases?
- ADHD?
- Athletic ability?

*Would you draw a line? Where?*

@citation

https://www.fertility-docs.com/programs-and-services/pgd-screening/choose-your-babys-eye-color/

@notes

These are real advertisements, not an endorsement or independent proof of accuracy.
The named clinics list US locations. Eye-color predictions depend on inherited variants and
available embryos; the advertised service does not guarantee a particular child or outcome.
This is selection before pregnancy, unlike prenatal testing and decisions during pregnancy.
The right-hand examples are discussion questions, not claims that any trait can reliably be chosen.
ADHD and athletic ability involve many genetic and environmental influences.
Ask what evidence would be needed before trusting a prediction for a complex trait.

